# 2. Non-negotiable invariant

Preserve the repository’s existing core invariant:

> Models never act directly. Models propose typed operations and structured artifacts. The trusted backend validates, persists, authorizes, applies, executes, rolls back, and audits all effects.

This invariant applies to every new role and mode.

No role may:

* write directly to repository files;
* execute unrestricted shell text;
* bypass RepoGuard;
* bypass patch validation;
* approve its own patch;
* apply raw frontend-provided patch content;
* manufacture approval records;
* select arbitrary checkpoint paths;
* run an unapproved command;
* merge into the active branch;
* alter the standing mandate governing Dream Mode;
* mark requirements verified without evidence;
* convert a neural risk score into authority;
* expose or claim to expose private chain-of-thought.

Visible agent traces must consist only of structured artifacts, decisions, concise rationale, questions, findings, evidence, and proposed actions.

Repository contents, model responses, generated prototypes, command output, test output, and external text are untrusted inputs.

