# 6. Required roles

All roles must use isolated logical sessions and role-specific context bundles.

The same local model endpoint may serve multiple roles sequentially. Do not require multiple 80B models to be resident simultaneously.

Support per-role runtime configuration, but provide a safe default that reuses one configured local runtime.

## 6.1 Dreamer

Purpose:

* identify overlooked opportunities;
* propose adjacent, strategic, and moonshot futures;
* synthesize repeated friction, failures, technical debt, and product context;
* generate falsifiable opportunity hypotheses;
* propose the smallest useful experiment.

The Dreamer must not:

* approve its own idea;
* create an implementation goal directly;
* modify code;
* conceal counterarguments;
* treat novelty as value.

Required output:

* one or more validated Dream Contracts.

## 6.2 Forward-Deployed Engineer

Use the display name **Forward-Deployed Engineer** and short label **FDE**.

Purpose:

* own the connection between business context and technical delivery;
* uncover the underlying problem beneath the requested solution;
* challenge whether code is needed;
* create objectives and outcome hypotheses;
* distinguish facts from requirements, inferences, assumptions, and unknowns;
* evaluate Dream Contracts;
* select or reject opportunities;
* define value, constraints, and non-goals;
* review whether implementation still serves the approved outcome;
* trigger replanning when assumptions fail.

The FDE must be able to recommend:

* proceed;
* run a smaller experiment;
* simplify;
* defer;
* reject the feature;
* reframe the goal.

Required output:

* FDE brief;
* objective;
* outcome hypothesis;
* assumption register;
* constraints;
* non-goals;
* promoted or rejected opportunity decision.

## 6.3 UX Designer

Purpose:

* translate the objective into a coherent user experience;
* generate competing UX directions when appropriate;
* produce a declarative interactive prototype;
* define behavior, not merely appearance;
* define accessibility and recovery behavior;
* compare the running implementation with the approved UX Contract.

Required outputs:

* UX Contract;
* declarative prototype document;
* UX acceptance criteria;
* post-implementation UX conformance report.

The UX role may not execute generated arbitrary UI code in the trusted app.

## 6.4 Skeptic / Product Red Team

Purpose:

* search for unsupported value claims;
* challenge solution-first reasoning;
* detect renamed duplicates of previous ideas;
* identify maintenance, security, complexity, and adoption risks;
* propose cheaper disconfirming experiments;
* challenge prototypes that look compelling but lack evidence;
* identify when agents are reinforcing one another without independent evidence.

Required outputs:

* blocking and non-blocking findings;
* disconfirmation experiment;
* recommendation of `REJECT`, `REVISE`, `EXPERIMENT`, or `PROCEED`.

The Skeptic cannot permanently veto work by itself. Blocking findings route to the FDE or human according to policy.

