The Planner must not rewrite the objective to match implementation convenience.

Required outputs:

* specification version;
* requirements;
* acceptance criteria;
* task graph;
* validation plan.

## 6.7 Builder

Purpose:

* implement exactly one bounded task or explicitly grouped atomic task set;
* inspect necessary repository context;
* propose typed patch operations;
* respond to concrete reviewer and verifier findings;
* publish beliefs and uncertainties.

The Builder must not:

* approve or apply its own patch;
* weaken tests to hide failure;
* expand scope silently;
* rewrite requirements;
* mark itself complete based only on plausibility.

## 6.8 Verifier

Purpose:

* independently derive requirement-level verification;
* run approved deterministic checks;
* generate independent tests when needed;
* detect test gaming;
* inspect actual evidence;
* distinguish implementation presence from correct behavior.

The Verifier should not receive unnecessary Builder commentary before independently deriving its verification plan.

Required output:

```json
{
  "verdict": "PASS",
  "requirementEvidence": [],
  "missingEvidence": [],
  "failures": [],
  "suspectedTestGaming": [],
  "recommendedNextAction": "REVIEW"
