# 7. Orchestration loop

Implement a persisted, resumable state machine.

The normal delivery loop is:

```text
User prompt or promoted Dream
  → FDE discovery
  → Dreamer alternatives when applicable
  → Skeptic challenge
  → UX concepts and contract
  → architecture alternatives
  → approved objective/spec boundary
  → Planner task graph
  → scope approval
  → isolated implementation workspace
  → Builder task
  → typed-operation validation
  → approval according to active policy
  → transactional apply
  → governed validation
  → independent Verifier
  → Reviewer
      PASS    → next task or final candidate
      REVISE  → targeted Builder feedback
      REPLAN  → Planner/FDE/Architect as appropriate
      BLOCKED → human or designated role intervention
  → final UX review
  → final FDE outcome-alignment review
  → proof-carrying change set
  → human merge review
```

## 7.1 Frozen specifications

Once implementation begins, a specification version is immutable.

Corrections create a new version.

A `REVISE` verdict does not modify the spec.

A `REPLAN` verdict creates a proposed new version and explains:

* what evidence invalidated the current plan;
* which requirements or assumptions changed;
* what tasks are invalidated;
* whether applied work remains valid;
* whether rollback is required.

## 7.2 Completion rule

An initiative may become implementation-complete only when:

* every required task passed;
* all mandatory validation commands passed;
* every approved requirement has sufficient evidence;
* no blocking verifier finding remains;
* no blocking reviewer finding remains;
* no blocking UX finding remains;
* no blocking architecture-conformance finding remains;
* the final diff remains inside approved scope;
* the active spec and ADR versions match the reviewed versions;
* the worktree is clean except for the proposed change set;
* budget limits were not exceeded;
* the proof-carrying report was generated.

Implementation completion must remain distinct from outcome confirmation.

## 7.3 No-progress detection

Stop automatic repair and transition to `BLOCKED` or `REPLAN` when any configured condition occurs, including:

* the same blocking finding repeats three times;
* the same files are repeatedly changed and reverted;
* a test alternates between pass and failure across iterations;
* diff size grows without increased requirement coverage;
* no requirement gains evidence across the configured event window;
* the Builder repeatedly violates the same ADR;
* the Builder modifies unrelated files;
* validation score fails to improve;
* repeated patches recreate behavior previously rejected;
* the task exceeds its iteration, time, file, or compute budget.

Provide a visible explanation.

Never implement an immortal loop.

