* use fake data;
* run approved local build/test commands;
* generate prototype evidence;
* iterate within budgets.

Forbidden:

* active working-tree modification;
* active branch merge;
* network by default;
* credentials;
* real user data;
* package installation unless the mandate explicitly allows a separately governed installation workflow;
* publishing externally.

### Level 3: Incubator

Allowed only when explicitly enabled:

* continue bounded evidence-based improvement of an approved prototype;
* run Builder/Verifier/Reviewer loops;
* compare alternatives;
* create a final candidate.

Still forbidden:

* autonomous merge;
* push;
* release;
* deployment;
* mutation of the user’s active working tree;
* modification of the governing mandate.

Dream Mode must favor learning over feature quantity.

