* A final proof-carrying report is produced.

## UX

* The UX role produces a validated declarative prototype.
* The prototype is interactive using fake local state.
* It cannot execute arbitrary code or access privileged APIs.
* UX acceptance criteria are linked to implementation evidence.
* UX can issue post-implementation findings.

## Dream

* Dream Mode requires a standing mandate.
* Ideation can run without changing code.
* Candidates enter Dream Inbox.
* Candidates can be rejected or promoted.
* Prototype implementation occurs only in an isolated worktree.
* Budgets are enforced.
* Active branch and merge remain human-controlled.
