## Intent and evidence

* Objectives, assumptions, constraints, requirements, ADRs, tasks, operations, and evidence are persistently linked.
* Invalidated assumptions are visible.
* Requirements cannot become verified without evidence.
* Historical spec versions remain immutable.

## Pulse

* Deterministic drift monitors work.
* Belief divergence works.
* Pulse interventions are bounded proposals.
* Rule-based temporal monitoring is the production default.
* The experimental liquid observer updates by elapsed time and supports snapshot/restore.
* Uncalibrated liquid weights cannot enable active authority.
* Neural outputs are clearly labeled experimental.
* Pulse never approves or verifies work.

## Security

* Worktree operations are backend owned.
* Models cannot forge lifecycle state.
* Models cannot merge.
* Models cannot bypass typed operations.
* Models cannot run arbitrary shell commands.
* Generated UX cannot execute arbitrary code in the trusted UI.
* Standing-mandate and budget bypasses are tested.
